// Package pycompat holds the Python 3.15 behaviour the ported tools must reproduce byte for
// byte: repr()/str() of values, float repr and "%g", int()/float() parsing, %-formatting
// with a mapping, the str predicates (isalpha, isdecimal, isdigit, isnumeric, isalnum,
// isprintable, isspace, re's \w) from tables generated by the Python itself, strip/split/
// splitlines, bytes.decode("utf-8", "replace"), html.escape/unescape and posixpath helpers.
//
// testdata/gen.py (run with python3 -I) writes unicode.txt and testdata/fixtures.json; the
// tests replay every fixture and hash every code point against Python's digests.
package pycompat
